CORROSION. 

WITH INDIAN FORCES NOT GIVING UP AND THE FIELD LITTERED WITH 
THE REMAINS OF 2ND PLT/ECHO, 1ST PLT HAS BEEN ORDERED ON IT'S 
FINAL MISSION.

ASSUMING A COURSE HEADING OF 136ø SOUTH BY SOUTH EAST, ECHO-1 IS 
TO SANCTION ANY COMMUNICATIONS LINKS WITHIN THE INDIAN CONTROLLED 
ZONE. THIS WILL LEAD YOUR PLT TO THE ENEMY'S COMMAND ENCAMPMENT. 
SANCTION ALL ELEMENTS WITHIN THE ENEMY COMPOUND.

THE REMAINING UNITS OF 2ND PLT. ARE ORDERED TO CONTINUE ALONG 
THEIR COURSE HEADING OF 186ø IN SUPPORT OF ECHO-1. SHOULD ECHO-1 
FAIL IN IT'S MISSION OBJECTIVE, ECHO-2 IS AUTHORIZED TO COMPLETE 
ALL REMAINING TASKS.

